// idem_boot -- the entry point a packed game's main.id calls.
//
//     main(int argc, string[] argv) { … } return int idem_boot(chunks, argc, argv);
//
// The packer has generated that call all along and it has been satisfied by a
// stub in the round-trip test. This is the real one.
//
// In: the game's sources as chunks, joined once. Out: the process exit code, and
// a window in between.
//
// The init order is the engine's and is not negotiable -- an exported global does
// not exist until its declaring function has run. Trigonometry before anything
// that takes a sine, the arena before anything that parses, the surface before
// anything that measures itself against one.

// One argument of any kind means `--shot`: render a single frame and write the
// surface to stdout as a PPM instead of opening a loop. It is the verification
// path ARCHITECTURE.md §10 describes, it needs no display, and it is the only way
// to check what a game draws without a person looking at it.
idem_boot(string[] chunks, int argc, string[] argv) {
  idem_init();
  err_mute(0);
  idem_read(run_join(chunks, 0, ""));
} return int idem_go(argc, argv);

idem_init() {
  fx_trig_init();
  rnd_init(20260730);
  idem_init2();
} return void;

idem_init3() {
  d2_spr_init();
  ent_init();
  idem_init5();
} return void;
